#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:1
msgid ""
"Ensures rST underlines (===, ---, etc.) are at least as long as the "
"preceding text."
msgstr ""
"Соответствует underline-шаблону RST, который содержит подчеркивание (===, "
"---, и т. д.), не менее длины предыдущего текста."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:3
#: readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:3
msgid "The rST text."
msgstr ""
".. _ translators' guide \n"
"\n"
"Translator's Guide\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
"Introduction\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"As a translator, your primary goal is to create accurate and readable content for your target audience.\n"
"\n"
"### Best Practices\n"
"\n"
"*   **Understand the context**: Before translating, make sure you understand the context and nuances of the source text.\n"
"*   **Use precise terminology**: Use the most accurate and precise terminology available in both languages to avoid confusion.\n"
"*   **Be aware of cultural differences**: Be sensitive to cultural differences and idioms that may not translate directly.\n"
"\n"
"Translation Tips\n"
"----------------\n"
"\n"
"### Translation Guidelines\n"
"\n"
"*   **Words for words**: Translate words literally, unless they have multiple meanings or connotations that are culturally specific.\n"
"*   **Idioms and expressions**: Use idiomatic translations when possible, but be aware of potential cultural nuances.\n"
"*   **Technical terminology**: Use technical terminology consistently throughout the document.\n"
"\n"
"Troubleshooting\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"### Common Challenges\n"
"\n"
"*   **Homophones**: When encountering homophones (words with similar pronunciations), choose the translation that best fits the context and intended meaning.\n"
"*   **Cultural references**: Be aware of cultural references that may not translate directly, such as idioms or colloquialisms.\n"
"\n"
"Conclusion\n"
"----------\n"
"\n"
"By following these guidelines and being mindful of cultural differences, you can create accurate and readable content for your target audience."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:4
msgid "The rST text with fixed underlines."
msgstr ""
".. _fixed_underlines:\n"
"\n"
"Fixed Underlines\n"
"================\n"
"\n"
"Fixed underlines are used to draw horizontal lines underneath specific parts of a table or other element. They can be used for visual separation, grouping elements together, and providing additional context.\n"
"\n"
"Creating Fixed Underlines\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"To create fixed underlines in RST, you can use the following syntax:\n"
"\n"
".. _fixed_underline: *\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"```rst\n"
"+=========+\n"
"|  Hello  |\n"
"+=========+\n"
".. _fixed_underline: * \n"
"This is a fixed underline\n"
"`````````````````````````\n"
"Fixed Underlines in Tables\n"
"--------------------------\n"
"\n"
"You can also apply fixed underlines to table headers or rows using the following syntax:\n"
"\n"
"| Column 1 | Column 2 |\n"
"|----------|----------|\n"
"| Cell 1   | Cell 2    |\n"
"| _header_ | _row2_   |\n"
"| Cell 3   | Cell 4    |\n"
"\n"
"In this example, `_header_` and `_row2_` are the parts of the table that will have fixed underlines."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:1
msgid "Replaces rST-specific syntax with placeholders to prevent translation."
msgstr ""
"Правит rST-сpezифический синтаксис с placeholders для предотвращения "
"перевода."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:4
